  "keyTakeaways": [
    "U.S. exports of steel articles fell 5.1% to $21.82B in 2025; other articles (7326, $6.41B) and fasteners (7318, $5.63B) are 55% of the total.",
    "Canada, the second-largest buyer at $5.81B (down 13.2%), charges a 50% surtax on most U.S. steel articles since September 8, 2026, CUSMA or not; stoves, radiators, kitchenware, sinks and leaf springs pay 25%, and cast-iron pipe is the one product with no surtax at all.",
    "Mexico ($7.32B) charges nothing on goods that meet the USMCA rule of origin, but since January 1, 2026 its general rate on many steel lines is 35%, so failing the rule is now expensive.",
    "The EU charges nothing on U.S. steel articles since July 1, 2026, but it can restore duties on chapters 72, 73 and 76 after December 31, 2026, and pipe and tube still pay 50% above the EU steel quota."
  ],
